🔧 Detailed Error Resolution Steps
Error #1: Gradle Version 9.6 Does Not Exist
Symptom:

Error: Gradle version 9.6 does not exist
  at gradleRelease (/home/runner/work/_actions/gradle/actions/v4/dist/setup-gradle/main/index.js:159154:15)
  at async Object.provisionGradle (...)
Root Cause: 

Gradle 9.6 is not published to official Gradle repositories
Version 9.x requires AGP (Android Gradle Plugin) 9.0+, which may have compatibility issues
Resolution Steps:

Identify Current Version

cat android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties | grep distributionUrl
Choose Compatible Version

Gradle 8.4 (RECOMMENDED)
- Compatible with AGP 8.0-8.2
- Latest stable in 8.x series
- Proven production stability

OR

Gradle 8.5+
- If project requires AGP 9.0+
- Newer but less battle-tested
Update gradle-wrapper.properties

sed -i 's|gradle-9.6|gradle-8.4|g' \
  android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
Verify the Change

grep "distributionUrl" android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
# Expected output:
# distributionUrl=https\://services.gradle.org/distributions/gradle-8.4-bin.zip
Update Android Gradle Plugin (if needed)

// android/build.gradle
plugins {
  id 'com.android.application' version '8.4.0' apply false  // Changed from 9.6
}
Clean and Rebuild

cd android
./gradlew clean
./gradlew assembleDebug --info
Error #2: Dependencies Lock File Not Found
Symptom:

Error: Dependencies lock file is not found in /home/runner/work/SuberTube/SuberTube
Supported file patterns: package-lock.json, npm-shrinkwrap.json, yarn.lock
Root Cause:

package.json exists but package-lock.json was not committed to repository
Lock file prevents dependency version floating (security & reproducibility)
Resolution Steps:

Verify Node.js Environment

node --version      # Should be v20.20.2 or compatible
npm --version       # Should match package.json engines
Locate package.json

find . -name "package.json" -type f
# Typically in: ./web/package.json or root
Generate Lock File

cd <directory-with-package.json>

# Option A: Create lock file without installing (preferred)
npm ci --package-lock-only

# Option B: Install with lock file (if Option A fails)
npm install --legacy-peer-deps
Verify Lock File

ls -la package-lock.json
# Should exist and be valid JSON

# Validate JSON structure
python3 -m json.tool package-lock.json > /dev/null && echo "Valid JSON"
Commit to Repository

git add package-lock.json
git commit -m "🔒 Add package-lock.json for reproducible builds"
git push origin bugfix/missing-dependencies-lock
Create PR for Review

Title: "🔒 Fix: Missing dependencies lock file"
Body: Explain security benefits and reproducibility
Labels: [dependencies, security, critical]
